I've now fully traced the flow. Here's my analysis and proposed implementation.

## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
Persist the last URL a user visited inside an app iframe so that when `AppWindow` is re-created (panel reopen / layout restore), the iframe starts on that URL instead of the app's default path.

**What's already in place (from the provided context)**
- `AppWindow.created()` already restores `this.params.params.lastUrl || app.path`.
- `AppWindow.persistUrl()` already calls `ui.updateAppParams(...)`.
- `store/ui.js → updateAppParams()` already merges into `openApps[tabId].params`, syncs the dockview `panel.params`, and triggers `onLayoutChanged()` so it lands in the persisted layout (`views.js`).
- `AppWindow` already binds `@navigated="onNavigated"`.

**The real gap**
`Iframe.vue` **never emits `navigated`**. So:
1. The whole navigation-persistence path is dead code.
2. In-app navigations (SPA `pushState` / hash changes) don't fire the iframe `load` event, so they are never captured.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- If the iframe starts emitting `navigated` on every in-app navigation, and `AppWindow` writes that url back into `currentUrl` (which is bound to the iframe `src`), Vue would re-assign `iframe.src` → **full reload of the app on every navigation**. So the tracked url must be kept separate from the `src`.
- Polling `contentWindow` is only possible for same-origin frames; cross-origin access throws, so tracking must stop quietly.
- Vue 3 project (`vue@^3.5.29`) → lifecycle hook is `beforeUnmount`.

**Target Files**
| File | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| `src/components/Iframe.vue` | Modify — emit `navigated` on load + in-app navigation |
| `src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue` | Modify — keep `src` stable, track `lastUrl` for persistence |

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

1. **`Iframe.vue`** — emit `navigated` with the current url/title. Emit once after load and then poll (1s) to catch in-app navigations; stop on cross-origin or unmount.
2. **`AppWindow.vue`** — introduce a non-`src` `lastUrl` used only for dedup/persistence, so the iframe is never reloaded by the tracking.

No change is needed to `src/store/ui.js` — `updateAppParams` already persists and syncs to the dockview layout.

## 3. File changes

```vue src/components/Iframe.vue
<template>
  <iframe ref="iframe" :src="url" class="bg-base-300" 
    @load="onIframeLoaded"
    title="coder" allow="camera *;microphone *;clipboard-read; clipboard-write;">
  </iframe>
</template>
<script>
export default {
  props: ['url', 'nocheck'],
  emits: ['loaded', 'navigated'],
  data() {
    return {
      trackedUrl: null,
      urlCheckInterval: null
    }
  },
  beforeUnmount() {
    this.stopUrlTracking()
  },
  methods: {
    onIframeLoaded() {
      const { iframe } = this.$refs
      if (!iframe?.contentWindow) {
        return setTimeout(() => this.onIframeLoaded, 2000)
      }
      // Track in-app (SPA) navigations that don't fire a `load` event
      this.startUrlTracking()
      if (this.nocheck) {
        return this.$emit('loaded', iframe)
      }
      this.$emit('loaded', iframe)
    },
    // Emit `navigated` whenever the iframe url changes (same-origin only)
    trackNavigation() {
      try {
        const contentWindow = this.$refs.iframe?.contentWindow
        const url = contentWindow?.location?.href
        if (!url || url === 'about:blank') return
        if (url === this.trackedUrl) return
        this.trackedUrl = url
        this.$emit('navigated', url, contentWindow?.document?.title)
      } catch (e) {
        // Cross-origin access blocked, stop polling
        this.stopUrlTracking()
      }
    },
    startUrlTracking() {
      this.trackNavigation()
      if (!this.urlCheckInterval) {
        this.urlCheckInterval = setInterval(() => this.trackNavigation(), 1000)
      }
    },
    stopUrlTracking() {
      if (this.urlCheckInterval) {
        clearInterval(this.urlCheckInterval)
        this.urlCheckInterval = null
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

